    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d645">

                <pb facs="0969" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg841"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 645.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Wallace</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 268.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 466, of the 24th ultimo, reporting conversations with the minister of
                    foreign affairs and the grand vizier respecting the proposed new treaty of
                    commerce between Turkey and the United States.</p>
                <p>This Government is as much interested as Turkey in removing all causes of
                    misapprehension, and if it will benefit our pending reclamations you may assure
                    the Porte of the good disposition of this Government.</p>
                <p>Further report will, however, be awaited before definitely instructing you to
                    make a new tariff and treaty.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
